{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/393614-what-does-the-courts-do","id":393614,"title":"What does the Courts do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-05T03:51:37-08:00","id":393614,"title":"What does the Courts do?","content":"<br /> Continuing my streak of having others explain the fundamentals of the game I would now like to know what the Courts spend their time and resources on.<br /> <br /> What are the Courts general program or what do they spend their budget on? I imagine they try to keep som shared Hollow going? And they educate and care for each other certainly. But do they have any long-time goals? Kindred I believe spend huge amount of energy fighting amongst themselves, is this the same with changelings generally?<br /> <br /> Do people usually envision the Courts as more of a political party, that will just create new goals as soon as they reach the old ones? Or do the Courts usually just try to cover the basics and serve as a platform for it's members and their ambitions?<br /> <br /> I know that this might be one of those questions like &quot;how long is a piece of string?&quot; that has a ridiculus amount of answers... But I really liked hearing what other's have to say about some of the basic elements of the setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T05:02:13-08:00","id":393653,"title":"","content":"I think of the courts as being mostly like a mutual aid society. They help newly arrived Changelings get their feet and then provide a support network of folks who know what you are going through and you can talk to without sounding crazy. Each court has their own vision of how to help folks. The Spring Court helps you get integrated back into human society, the Winter Court helps you find a place to hide, etc. Some are very benevolent, running under a &quot;pay it forward&quot; mentality. Some are all about trading of favors and keeping track of obligations. You OWE the guy who helps you get a new identity and a job when you arrive. Each Court has an agenda beyond this that they pursue and which court members are expected to contribute. The Autumn Court researches magic and the True Fae, the Summer Court trains its folks to fight and patrols the Hedge, etc.<br /> <br /> I'm very interested to see 2nd edition's take on things as it sounds like they are adding a whole new layer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T05:32:47-08:00","id":393665,"title":"","content":"As with many things in the World of Darkness, the answer varies from city to city. Assuming a &quot;baseline&quot; city that's actually working as intended and that hasn't been distracted by pointless (or &quot;pointless&quot; but actually vital, Pledge-wise) trivia, the courts as a whole:<br /> <br /> * Serve as a governing body for the city, through the framework of the rotating monarchy<br /> * Locate, protect, teach, and watch over newly-returned Lost, helping them find their feet after the chaos of Arcadia<br /> * Monitor their members (and occasionally the members of other Courts) for signs of severe Clarity loss and insanity, and work to help those who've fallen to madness (or destroy them if they can no longer be helped).<br /> <br /> In a Seasonal freehold, the individual Courts have other aims and methods. <br /> <br /> Summer:<br /> * Trains and equips members of the Freehold for when martial defense is necessary.<br /> * Serves as protectors and sometimes police for the Freehold.<br /> * Maintains ties to mortal groups of combatants (police, gangs, militias) to make use of as needed.<br /> <br /> Autumn:<br /> * Monitors for omens, signs, and mystical evidence of the Others or other supernatural threats.<br /> * Studies the Others, keeping track of weaknesses and powers in case the Freehold comes up against one.<br /> * Collects magical knowledge and trinkets for a rainy day (or to keep them out of other hands).<br /> <br /> Winter:<br /> * Maintains safe houses, supply depots, and bolt holes throughout the city in case evacuation is needed.<br /> * Serves as a Changeling CIA, acting in secret to ferret out and destroy enemies of the Court and the Freehold. <br /> * Scouts and monitors the surrounding area to act as an early-warning system.<br /> <br /> Spring:<br /> * Maintains the morale of the Freehold (not as simple a job as it sounds given the Lost).<br /> * Keeps and develops ties in mortal society in order to gather resources and allies in case of emergency.<br /> * Serves as a corps of diplomats and negotiators in times of need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T12:15:53-08:00","id":394015,"title":"","content":"Social organizations and support groups. You might say ones that have 'gone wild.' You've been through a horrible situation, but so have most other changelings. Everyone has different ways of coping with it, but it's the kind of thing that must be coped with. One Spring Court may just hold small parties every week. Another may sponsor concerts and get involved with sporting events in an alliance with the summer court. Changeling is really a neat game like that, you can go as far as you want or keep things close and intimate.<br /> <br /> And you mentioned this in the other thread, about changelings trying to promote emotions of their court so they can harvest it. Some might, but it's not really something you would see every court doing. Changelings can get glamour from any emotion, and mechanically the difference between the court emotion and any other is a single die if you're not using merits. The books are really good at exploring this, I found. They tend to explain the variety you would see in courts and freeholds, complete with samples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T14:45:01-08:00","id":394134,"title":"","content":"Everyone above has done a great job describing the practical, day-by-day functions and objectives of the individual Courts, along with how they provide a support network for the Lost. I'll do my best to summarise one of the most confusing and vaguely defined aspects of the Courts: their metaphysical defence against the Fae.<br /> <br /> First off: the metaphysical, the imaginary, the conceptual... These things are all &quot;real&quot; for the inhabitants of Arcadia. It's one of the reasons that they seem insane to mortal beings, who draw a line between reality and the imagined. To a degree, the Hedge *is* that line; it's a metaphor for the line between the world and imagination... and since Arcadia sees no difference between the two, it's a physically manifest metaphor.<br /> <br /> Back on topic. The Court system is described in the core books as a means of confusing and defending against the Fae. While the Summer Court carries out an obvious role in this function, simply having the system itself is described as weakening the Gentry's influence in the world.<br /> <br /> Here are some perspectives to explain why:<br /> <br /> - Allying one's self to a season is tied intrinsically to the Real World. The division between &quot;real&quot; and &quot;imaginary&quot; is reinforced by the regular, immutable fact that the earth rotates in a fixed pattern, resulting in a progression of regular weather patterns for a good area of the planet. That this is something that is not only accepted but embraced by changelings confuses the Fae, who have complete control over their environment within Faerie.<br /> <br /> - The passing on of power. The leadership of the Freehold is tied to this progression of seasons, with each monarch passing the reins to another at each shift. This further confuses the Gentry, since absolute power is essential to their being. The idea that other people even exist, let alone deserve to posess power, is a challenge to them.<br /> <br /> -Belonging. As has been pointed out, having a group to look out for you is especially important for the Lost: it replaces the life and home that has been lost. Each changeling that finds a purpose greater than themselves, that is worth becoming a part of, starts to get over the damage and hurt that they've experienced. Mutual benefit, community, being part of a greater cause... none of these things make sense to an all-powerful solipsist. The Fae only recognise themselves and their absolute control.<br /> <br /> So, okay, these ideas confuse them. So what? How is that not just extra incentive to punch a hole in reality and start a massacre?<br /> <br /> Well, it all goes back to the first point: the True Fae don't see a difference between ideas and reality in the same way mortals do. Ideas that are anathema to their existence (compassion, consideration of others, the acceptance of being powerless) are as real and imposing as rocks and iron. More so, even. Imagine having the ability to see for miles and in the deepest darkness but that anybody who is performing a kind deed is blurred, even invisible. Imagine being able to ignore the laws of distance and time, going anywhere, but the idea of friendship blocks you like a wall.<br /> <br /> The Gentry hate that. So, sometimes, they get clever. Send in some Loyalists to shake up the system, sowing distrust. Start grabbing children from the street where the Spring Queen lives, ramping up the fear. Offer an unimportant changeling unimaginable wealth in exchange for dark secrets. Greed, fear, distrust, struggles for power: these are concepts that are familiar and comfortable to Them. They glide through those concepts like clear water.<br /> <br /> Cutting my ramble there. I'm sure I had more points... well, I could talk all day on this. Hope it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T17:33:53-08:00","id":394299,"title":"","content":"In general, I use the Courts as one part social organization, one part mutual defense, one part laws and punishment. They tend to be less oppressive than Vampiric organizations...one need not present themselves to the reigning monarch. However, doing so once found tends to be a smart move, as those outside the organization tend to be distrusted.<br /> <br /> In my head to some degree I view the Courts as more like college, or possibly being within the gay subculture. There are major movers and shakers the outside world knows little of, a whole significant social circle even if you are not a part of it, neat people around every corner, and a world you often find yourself sort of thrust into. There are elements that don't necessarily match up, like the monarch (though it can...) but some unusual traditions and an odd sense of camaraderie based more on experiences than common interest sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T04:43:42-08:00","id":401738,"title":"","content":"Seasonal Courts have colors +Many Courts are working together + Rainbow has many colors + Rainbow is symbol of LGBT subculture =&gt; Seasonal Courts are gay subculture! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T12:29:24-08:00","id":402246,"title":"","content":"The GLBT connection was stronger with Dreaming, but yea that is fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T12:18:42-08:00","id":408048,"title":"","content":"Alright thanks, a lot of good answers once again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Never thought before about how many things I just suppose about the different factions in nWoD, learning a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T12:35:26-08:00","id":408067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Imagine having the ability to see for miles and in the deepest darkness but that anybody who is performing a kind deed is blurred, even invisible. Imagine being able to ignore the laws of distance and time, going anywhere, but the idea of friendship blocks you like a wall. &quot; </div> </div> </div>Dammit, if only were possible to weaponize friendship into a super weap....<br /> ...you know, forget that. I didn\u00b4t say anything. Let\u00b4s move along.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T16:36:11-08:00","id":413364,"title":"","content":"One of the things that first brought Changeling to my attention was how people had made the connection of the Courts and survivors of severe traumatic events/PTSD sufferers. <br /> <br /> The Courts are defined by something deeper than their function, they are defined by the reactions people have to their victimhood, because Changelings aren't just changed in their bodies, alone. This results in pathological behaviors of one form or another, and while the different changelings may recognize them as madness from time to time, Courts JUSTIFY the pathologies. They're people like you, who went through what you went through, and not only react like you react, but tell you about how your fly-off-the-handle overreactions to certain things aren't just the hair-trigger ingrained response of a lunatic, but somehow totally necessary to save everyone you know and love from a fate worse than death. <br /> <br /> Consider the following for each season:<br /> <br /> Winter -<br /> If you ever watched the movie Munich, at the start of the movie, the main character and one of the other cell members sent out by the Mossad to hunt down Islamic terrorist group Black September are rookies and make fun of the veterans, and one guy mentions how he knew one guy who never slept in his bed. He slept in the closet, and stuffed pillows in his bed so that assassins would attack that first. They had a good laugh.<br /> <br /> Then, of course, the cell is exposed, they're disavowed, and the members of the cell are picked off one-by-one with bombs in their workshops or murdered in their sleep. And you know it, there's a scene where the main character looks at his bed, then the closet, and decides it's more comfortable in the closet, after all.<br /> <br /> The Winter court may say it's emotion is sorrow, but that's just what they eat. Their REAL court emotion is fear, because fear rules every thought in their head. Like a frightened herbivore, there is only one thought in their head: How do I make it through one more day? How do I keep from exposing myself to my predators? You can't fight, there's nowhere to run, all you can do is hide. <br /> <br /> Who needs friends? People who have friends talk to their friends. And those friends usually have friends, and talk to those friends, too. Loose lips brings a Gentry to torture you some more. Friends are a liability. Stay safe. Stay alone. Cooperate only with those who know how to keep things frosty and below the table. <br /> <br /> <br /> Spring -<br /> My paternal grandparents lived through the Depression, and they took from it that you save everything for the lean times, and never spare a dime you don't have to. They kept old margarine tubs around because you can reuse those, you know. They hand-made a lot of their own furniture from scraps they found from flea markets and wore clothes from the thrift store. <br /> <br /> My maternal grandparents had a very different experience: Take what you can take now, because it may all be gone tomorrow. Drink every penny you earn, because there's no point in a bank, that money will all vanish in a puff of smoke. <br /> <br /> This is what a Spring courtier is like. People always told you as a kid not to do reckless things and risk your future, but you know that it's all just a lie. You don't control your future, it's all the games of things way beyond your power. All you can choose is whether to have fun or not. You're probably going to die (or worse) when the Gentry find you, and they'll probably find you in minutes as soon as they remember to look, so you might as well have as much fun now while you still can. Why pretend you can exist forever like a Winter, when you never get to LIVE that way? <br /> <br /> Hey, let me do a little of whatever they're doing. Heh, you think drugs will ruin my future? There is no future. Might as well enjoy now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Summer -<br /> It was in your dreams again. The pain. The humiliation. The choke of the leash on your throat. The things you said when you begged, anything to make it stop. No! You don't want to remember. Anything to stop remembering! <br /> <br /> Then the hate takes over. Sweet, precious hate blinds you to the things you don't want to see and lets you delude yourself into thinking that NEXT TIME, it will be DIFFERENT. You can get up to your punching bag and make like you could REALLY make a difference next time, that you're not that pathetic little wretch that was paralyzed by the fear. You're IN CONTROL. Next time you see that THING, you're going to punch it! Just like that! No, don't stop to think about how you're going to actually pull that off, don't think of how powerful It is, just think of how strong you are now. No, better yet, STOP thinking, and just start punching things, because that makes you feel so much stronger, so much more in control of yourself and your future and did you see how good you look in the mirror? Yeah, check those abs. Yeah, you'll totally punch That Thing in the FACE next time. Then your pride will be AVENGED!<br /> <br /> Alternately, just think about the difference between Sarah Connor in the first and every other Terminator movie. How much of that was belief that dropping out of society to go to a mental institution and do pull-ups all day would really stop an army of robots, and how much was just the desperate attempt to do ANYTHING to try to give herself the illusion of being able to go toe-to-toe with the things in her nightmares?<br /> <br /> <br /> Autumn -<br /> Your eyes have been opened. You're through the Looking Glass now, you took the Red Pill, and now you can't unsee what you have seen. There's monsters out there. And you should know, because you're a monster now, too. There's no use denying it, or trying to go back to pretending the world is sane or fair. No point in hating the game, just learning how to play by its rules. <br /> <br /> You saw them do the impossible. Now, you're learning how to do the impossible, yourself. All the pain and the fear, you can quell it, bottle it, stuff it on the shelf if you can just focus on the dry facts of HOW. Think like a robot. Robots feel no pain. If you start to fear, just ask why and how, and how to replicate it in others, and use it against them. If you can turn the fear others cause in you against them, then it means you can use it against Them when the time comes. All their world revolves around secrets and hidden rules, and if you just find the right secret, you'll bow THEM to YOU! Every rare book just might be the one that gives you the weapon that slays your tormentor, and finally sets you free.<br /> <br /> In this world you can now see, everything's available to you, if you're willing to pay the price. There's nothing in this life that's free, but that doesn't mean you have to be the one that foots the bill. Sure, it's a bit unethical, it's something you wouldn't have considered before you saw this world, but there's lives at stake, now, and honestly, stealing someone else's treasured memories to buy the spear that will slay the beast coming to take their very families away from them? Well, that's an outright bargain for them, whether they know or consent to the deal or not. So what if stealing away with the precious things of others makes you just like the Others? That's another sacrifice worth making, and nothing worth having comes without some kind of sacrifice, right?<br /> <br /> You won't be like those blind fools in Spring or Summer, just making noise for their own sakes, you'll get things DONE. You aren't just hiding and hoping it doesn't happen to you again like the Winters. You're done being the prey, you're going to be the PREDATOR this time. You will learn to walk like the monster until you learn how to be a better monster than they are. When the Abyss stares back, they won't be able to see you anymore, for you will wear its own shadows so perfectly that they can't tell you apart from Them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you keep these shared pathologies and needs in mind, everything else spills out naturally from there. Summer justifies itself by saying it will fight... because fighting gives it the sense of control over its own destiny it so desperately needs to feel secure. Autumn justifies itself with its knowledge of the lore of the Hedge... because they are pathologically bound to finding knowledge of the arcane to feel they are in control of their world and their own fears, and to feel secure. Winter justifies itself with its secrecy and contingencies... because they're paranoid, and can't act without building quintuple redundancies into every failsafe just to try to feel like they're doing something about how vulnerable they are, and to feel secure. Spring justifies itself with its morale and diplomacy with mortals... because they have to dive into the realm of the mortals that don't know if they're to keep themselves from remembering that they do know what's out there, and only by forgetting how vulnerable they are do they ever feel secure.<br /> <br /> Everything else springs out of these basic driving pathologies. The court intrigues? Those are just lunatics fighting for control of the looney bin because they've thrown themselves so completely into their games of petty politics that they forgot they're still in their straightjackets. Better to fight the other loonies, who can't be more powerful than you, than the ones that threw you in there against your will, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"